Membership permissions contract migration requires coordinated downtime and irreversible confirmation.
Uppercase invite-code backfill (20260814000000) rewrites every stored invite code; binaries released
before it look invite codes up in lowercase and cannot resolve them, so the old color must be stopped
before the migration runs and is not a valid rollback target afterwards.
Text encryption removal (20261026000000) drops the E2ee* tables and ChatConversation.textEncryption;
binaries released before it still read and write them, so the old color must be stopped before the
migration runs and is not a valid rollback target afterwards.
